i appreciate you talking to me about  this i love this show on two levels it  has the nostalgia factor for me from  reading the books when i was younger and  it also proves that good stories and  good characters are universal no matter  your age  so what has it meant to you guys to get  to be a part of the babysitter's club  what's the coolest thing about being a  part of this world and doing this show  it's  yeah maybe it's your first time it's so  great um i know that mallory and jesse  loved it but annae and i also loved it  um because we got to just spend time  with those girls every day  and it was just it was a great  experience something that i've never  done so it was great yeah i'm so glad  that we got to bring these characters to  life  because like you said like the nostalgia  factor a lot of people have read these  books growing up and i'm so glad that we  can portray these characters on screen  and it's so cool to see everyone saying  like oh jesse was my favorite character  uh from the book series i can't wait to  see her in season two it's  i'm so happy to bring the character to  life  everybody  came back to this show and you guys you  know get added as members of the  babysitter's club this season so  were there nerves about  joining in that way  what reassured you  you know during your first day on set  i think that having a nay there was a  great  um  kind of like a  thing to bring my nerves down just  because we had both you know the other  cast had been shooting for many months  before us so when we came we were kind  of scared that we would you know not fit  in  um  so having an a there was was great to  just do it with someone and you know the  girls were welcoming so  yeah  season one like vivian said i was so  nervous coming on to set because all the  other girls knew each other already i i  felt a lot like jesse and mallory when  they joined the club because  um it's like i knew they were gonna be  nice but it's like are we gonna fit in  are we gonna not but just like jessie  and mallory we all the girls welcome  welcomed us in so much and they're our  best friends so coming on to film season  two was great and because we already  knew them all so well we've been texting  and facetiming for  months what does it mean to the  characters to be included as new  additions to the club what does it mean  to them to be able to take this  responsibility on  um jesse and mallory really look up to  the rest of the bsc um and in season one  you can see them say like they're like  world famous they're  valerie look out to them like they're  like celebrities so now that they're in  the club it's really surreal to them to  be in the club with like their idols  yeah jessie mallory are pretty star  struck  mallory definitely expresses it  a bit more but um  so i'm excited for the viewers to see  that what do you guys most enjoy about  working with this cast you get to do a  lot of big ensemble scenes together  what's the fun in getting to do those  and are they just really chaotic and  crazy  yeah i mean we're all  we're all best friends so we're all  super comfortable comfortable with each  other  so um the group scenes that we had in  claudia's room were definitely  some of my favorites um  we would you know  lunchtime during those days where we  would like do those scenes was always  the best because we would always sit  outside and kind of like a circle and  eat our lunch and talk and those are  some of my favorite days  yeah the scenes with all seven of us all  some seven of us were my favorite  because  i just love filming scenes with all of  us it did get a little crazy sometimes  because there were like seven teenage  girls on set all at once um and like  vivian said lunches were so fun um  especially towards towards the end of  filming we um like sat in the parking  lot and we like laid down blankets and  our coats and we all sat and ate lunch  together  what do you most love about your  character and what quality of theirs do  you wish you had yourself  um  i love my character because i love how  driven jessie is and her passion for  dance  um jessie's such a talented ballerina  and even though i play her um i wish you  know what i really wish i had her ballet  studio her ballet studio is so cool it  was one of my favorite sets to be on  because  oh my gosh jessie's so lucky that her  parents build that um ballet studio for  her and i'm def i definitely wish i had  that in my house  yeah um for me  um  mallory's siblings but i think they'd be  kind of cool it would be a little  chaotic um just because of you know she  has so many but i think having a good  variety of siblings would be fun because  i only have one in real life so  any i have to say i've been a dancer  since i was four and so i  really connect to jesse in that way and  i also would love to have had her whole  dance studio going on in my house but  what do you love about getting to  explore that side of her is there  anything that you did to prepare for  you know her dance ability  yeah um i've been doing ballet since i  was two years old so i would say i've  kind of been preparing my whole life for  this part but  even when i was in canada i would join  zoom classes with my ballet coach who  lives in london and i would just do my  ballet classes every morning and when i  didn't have time to do that i would do  ballet youtube videos so i could really  be prepared for this part because dance  is such a big part of jessie's life and  the dance scenes were definitely some of  my favorite scenes to film besides the  meetings  did you guys  feel like did you have moments that you  really sort of felt like you connected  to the character when things really  clicked when you really had an  understanding of who they were  definitely um at the beginning  um it was kind of hard to  develop  mallory as a character  so at the beginning i had to really  think  about how mallory would  act in the scene or act in the situation  or say this line because mallory and i  differ in a lot of ways and so  at the end of season two i was able to  read a line and just immediately know  how mallory would say it  and how she would act in that scene so  that was really fun for me to see how  her character development went  yeah jessie was such a fun character to  play because she's a lot like me  so  i think um jessie this season she really  struggles with her confidence and she  pushes herself to always try to be the  best and she puts a lot of pressure on  herself  and i honestly relate to that with her  because with like acting and dancing  there's a lot of pressure  um and  jesse taught me that you know i'm just a  kid and i just have to just be myself  and i don't have to worry about the  future too much and i just have to live  life in the moment  i love the message that comes through  with the season in the episode with the  kid who's famous on social media about  how sometimes you just have to be a kid  and enjoy kid things and not have that  added stress and pressure  do you guys feel like you find a balance  between living your lives using social  media  also getting to be a kid but working in  an adult world do you feel like you  really sort of found a sense of that  balance or is it something you're always  working on  yeah i think that i'm still working on  it now i mean it's very different than a  lot of what my friends at home have to  deal with  i'm pretty lucky to have a good  you know to have the  cast be around my age so if i need any  help i can just come and talk to them  um but it definitely is a different  life that the cast is living and being a  child and you know working on this show  but i think we've all found our ways to  manage it  yeah um  balancing acting in school and just  being a normal kid is never something  that you can fully master i've been  doing it since i was five and i still  haven't really perfected it and  sometimes um it does get kind of  stressful sometimes but i just take a  step back and realize  why i'm doing in the first place i'm  doing it because i love to act and even  though it can get stressful um balancing  school and acting at the same time  i just make sure to push through because  i love to i love to act and that is  really my passion so  well you guys are great in this you're  perfect in this character everybody  isn't so perfect in all their roles i i  love watching you all together  especially in those big scenes it's so  much fun so i appreciate you talking to  me about this season it's such a great  season  thank you

